    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "Core idea",
      "text": "<b>por</b> looks <b>back</b> (cause, origin, exchange, route). <b>para</b> looks <b>forward</b> (goal, destination, deadline, recipient). <i>Trabajo por mi familia</i> (for their sake) vs <i>Trabajo para mi familia</i> (I work for them, e.g. in the family business)."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Set phrases"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "style": "plain",
      "widths": [
        5.6,
        5.6,
        5.8
      ],
      "head": [
        "With por",
        "With para",
        "English"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "por eso",
          "para eso",
          "that is why / for that"
        ],
        [
